{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "All four completed experiments use singleprofile, leaving the multiprofile dimension entirely unexplored. The evidence shows RNA (scvi_n200) is the dominant signal (0.520 acc) while image alone is weak (0.208), and multimodal adds only ~1.6% over RNA-only. The most important open question is whether aggregating multiple profiles (via avgpool) improves representation quality. config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) is a clean A/B comparison against config_009 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200), changing only the profile setting and adding avgpool aggregation. This isolates the multiprofile effect without confounding it with fusion strategy, image encoder, or model complexity. Under a tight budget, resolving whether multiprofile is beneficial at all—on the modality that carries most signal—is the highest-information next step before committing experiments to more complex multimodal+multi configurations."
}

